# Exam track — Theme: Musek — Sub-lesson 1: Vocabulary
# Sproochentest oral-exam topic. Target level ~B1 (authoring guideline only).
#
# Every sub-lesson mixes words AND sentences so each session alternates
# word-match and sentence-builder slots; the emphasis here is vocabulary.

@lesson M1.01 "Music Vocabulary"

@word d'Musek = the music
@word d'Lidder = the songs
@word de Sänger = the singer
@word de Museker = the musician
@word d'Band = the band
@word d'Genren = the genres
@word de Concert = the concert
@word de Festival = the festival
@word d'Volleksmusek = folk music
@word d'Gittar = the guitar
@word lauschteren = to listen
@word sangen = to sing
@word kennen = to know
@word d'Erënnerungen = the memories

@sentence
@lu Ech lauschteren all Dag gär Musek.
@en I like listening to music every day.
@distractor-lu sangen
@distractor-lu kucken
@distractor-en singing
@distractor-en watching

@sentence
@lu D'Band spillt haut e Concert op engem Festival.
@en The band is playing a concert at a festival today.
@distractor-lu Radio
@distractor-lu Schoul
@distractor-en radio
@distractor-en school

@sentence
@lu Ech kenne vill Genren, mee Volleksmusek hunn ech am léifsten.
@en I know many genres, but I like folk music the most.
@distractor-lu danzen
@distractor-lu Radio
@distractor-en dance
@distractor-en radio

@sentence
@lu De Museker spillt Gittar, mee hie kann net sangen.
@en The musician plays the guitar, but he cannot sing.
@distractor-lu Schoul
@distractor-lu Auto
@distractor-en school
@distractor-en car

@sentence
@lu Al Lidder brénge mir dacks Erënnerungen.
@en Old songs often bring back memories for me.
@distractor-lu sangen
@distractor-lu lauschteren
@distractor-en sing
@distractor-en listen
